I'd love to create a special dinner party with fascinating historical figures I'd enjoy engaging with -  

Aristotle at one table, with Plato's insightful theories;  

Elizabeth I would bring a regal flair;  

Leonardo da Vinci could add an artistic dimension;  

Charles Darwin and Mary Anning could engage in deep scientific discussion;  

Harriet Tubman and Sojourner Truth to talk about equality;  

Galileo Galilei and Isaac Newton discussing physics concepts.  

We'd need to make sure the conversation topics respected each person's era and beliefs.  

It reminds me of the famous John F Kennedy dinner party that included Aristotle, Alexander the Great, Benjamin Franklin and other notables who debated politics, philosophy and science.  

Such an evening would be both a cultural education and a celebration of great human minds.
